{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:13:59Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 58, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Spec: Edit a task title\n2\t\n3\tTaiga #2\n4\t\n5\t## Triage\n6\t\n7\t**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability, no existing behaviour changes. Single\n8\tcohesive cycle: one new backend route plus the frontend UI to drive it. Does\n9\tnot span enough architectural layers to warrant splitting (compare: Taiga #1\n10\twas frontend-only; this one adds one backend route + one store method + one\n11\tcomponent's edit state \u2014 normal size for one cycle).\n12\t\n13\t## Goal\n14\t\n15\tLet someone fix a mistyped task title in place, without deleting and\n16\tre-creating the task.\n17\t\n18\t## Acceptance criteria\n19\t\n20\t1. **Enter edit mode.** Given a task in the list, when the user activates\n21\t   editing on it, then the title is replaced with an editable input\n22\t   pre-filled with the task's current title.\n23\t2. **Save a valid edit.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits a\n24\t   new title that is non-empty after trimming, then the task's title is\n25\t   updated, the change is persisted (still present after a page reload), and\n26\t   edit mode closes showing the new title.\n27\t3. **Cancel discards changes.** Given a task in edit mode with a modified\n28\t   draft, when the user cancels, then the title reverts to its original\n29\t   value, no save request is sent, and edit mode closes.\n30\t4. **Empty title is rejected, not saved.** Given a task in edit mode, when\n31\t   the user submits a title that is empty or whitespace-only, then the save\n32\t   is rejected: the task's title is unchanged (never blanked), the user gets\n33\t   visible feedback that the title can't be empty, and they remain able to\n34\t   correct it without having lost their place.\n35\t5. **Oversized title is rejected.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user\n36\t   submits a title over 200 characters (the existing `TaskIn` limit used for\n37\t   create), then the save is rejected the same way create rejects it today,\n38\t   and the task's title is unchanged.\n39\t6. **Backend: successful update.** Given an existing task, when\n40\t   `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\"title\": \"<1-200 chars>\"}`, then\n41\t   it returns `200` with the updated `Task`, and a subsequent `GET\n42\t   /api/tasks` reflects the new title.\n43\t7. **Backend: missing task.** Given no task with that id, when `PATCH\n44\t   /api/tasks/{id}` is called, then it returns `404`.\n45\t8. **Backend: empty title.** Given an existing task, when `PATCH\n46\t   /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\"title\": \"\"}`, then it returns `422`\n47\t   and the stored title is unchanged.\n48\t\n49\t## Non-goals\n50\t\n51\t- No edit history or undo beyond the in-progress cancel.\n52\t- No multi-field bulk edit, no editing multiple tasks' titles at once.\n53\t- No new concurrency/conflict resolution beyond what already exists \u2014 a save\n54\t  against a task deleted by someone else surfaces as a `404` through the\n55\t  existing error banner (`App.jsx`'s `run()` \u2192 `setError`), same as\n56\t  completing or deleting an already-gone task does today.\n57\t- No character counter or other new max-length UI beyond reusing the\n58\t  existing 200-char backend validation.\n59\t\n60\t## Affected areas\n61\t\n62\t- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 add `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}` route (mirrors\n63\t  the existing `POST /api/tasks/{task_id}/done` route shape at lines 32-37).\n64\t- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 add `TaskStore.set_title(task_id, title)`,\n65\t  mirroring `set_done` (lines 30-35).\n66\t- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 no change; the new route reuses `TaskIn`\n67\t  (line 5-6) for its request body, same validation as create.\n68\t- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 add tests for the new route, following the\n69\t  existing `client` fixture pattern (success, 404, 422 empty title).\n70\t- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 add `updateTask(id, title)` issuing a `PATCH`,\n71\t  next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (lines 20-21).\n72\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 add per-task edit-mode state and\n73\t  the editable-input UI (currently renders `task-title` as plain text at\n74\t  line 15).\n75\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 add an `onEdit` handler wired through the\n76\t  existing `run()` helper (lines 33-40), same pattern as `onComplete` /\n77\t  `onDelete` (lines 54-55).\n78\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styles for the edit input and its save/cancel\n79\t  controls, extending the existing `.task` rules (lines 30-35).\n80\t\n81\tExact trigger affordance, save/cancel control placement, and any\n82\tkeyboard-shortcut behavior (e.g. Enter/Escape) beyond the input's minimum\n83\tsave/cancel actions are the ux-designer's call, not fixed here.\n84\t\n85\t## Edge cases\n86\t\n87\t- Empty title submitted \u2192 rejected, task unchanged (AC4).\n88\t- Whitespace-only title (`\"   \"`) \u2192 trimmed before validation, treated the\n89\t  same as empty (AC4). Trimming happens client-side before the request is\n90\t  sent, same as `AddTask.jsx` already does for creation (line 8).\n91\t- Cancel with a modified draft \u2192 reverts, no request sent (AC3).\n92\t- Save with the draft identical to the original title \u2192 treated as a normal\n93\t  save (a `PATCH` is still sent); not special-cased, since it's harmless and\n94\t  idempotent in this in-memory store.\n95\t- Title over 200 characters \u2192 rejected by existing `TaskIn` validation\n96\t  (AC5), surfaced to the user rather than failing silently.\n97\t- Task deleted by another client while being edited \u2192 save fails with `404`,\n98\t  surfaced through the existing error banner (see Non-goals).\n99\t- Editing a task that is already marked `done` \u2192 allowed; nothing in the\n100\t  request restricts editing to open tasks only (see Open Questions).", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014aBiQNdN51MVAQQ8Qd5wL4", "session_id": "e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c"}}
