{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:15:48Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 189, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "# Design: Edit a task title\n\nTaiga #2 \u00b7 consumes `docs/spec.md`\n\n## Conventions established (before designing anything)\n\n- No component library, no icon set, no design tokens file \u2014 plain CSS in\n  `frontend/src/App.css`, function components, hooks only.\n- Existing button style is a single neutral style (`button { border, white\n  bg, radius 5px }`) with no primary/secondary visual hierarchy \u2014 Done and\n  Delete look the same. Nothing today distinguishes \"safe\" vs \"destructive\"\n  by color.\n- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\n  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\n  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\n- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\n  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\n  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\n- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \u2014\n  `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` \u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\n- Existing color tokens in use: text `#16191c`, border `#ccd2d6`, error text\n  `#a3271d` on error bg `#fbe9e7`, muted `#6b7780`, card bg `#fff`, page bg\n  `#f6f7f8`.\n\n**Decision: introduce no new component, no new color, no new button style.**\nEverything below extends `TaskList.jsx` and `App.css` in place, per the\nspec's affected areas.\n\n## Interaction model\n\n`TaskList` owns edit state locally (per spec: \"per-task edit-mode state\"):\n\n```js\nconst [editingId, setEditingId] = useState(null)\nconst [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\nconst [validationError, setValidationError] = useState(null)\n```\n\n- **Enter edit mode** \u2014 click a task's `Edit` button \u2192\n  `setEditingId(task.id); setDraft(task.title); setValidationError(null)`.\n  The input autofocuses (`autoFocus` \u2014 safe here since it only fires on a\n  direct user click, not on page load).\n- **Opening edit on a different task** \u2014 clicking `Edit` elsewhere just calls\n  `startEdit` again; `editingId`/`draft` are overwritten, so the previous\n  row's unsaved draft is silently discarded. This *is* the resolution to the\n  spec's open question 2 (only one task edits at a time) \u2014 no confirmation\n  dialog, per the spec's stated default.\n- **Cancel** \u2014 `Cancel` button, or `Escape` in the input \u2192\n  `setEditingId(null); setValidationError(null)`. No request sent. The row\n  re-renders from `tasks` (untouched), so the original title reappears with\n  no extra revert logic needed.\n- **Save, empty/whitespace draft (AC4)** \u2014 submit handler trims the draft\n  first, same as `AddTask.jsx` line 8. If empty, **block before calling\n  `onEdit`**: `setValidationError(\"Title can't be empty.\")`, keep\n  `editingId` set, return. No request is sent, focus stays in the input\n  (it never lost focus), the draft the user typed is preserved so they can\n  fix it in place.\n- **Save, valid draft (AC2)** \u2014 trimmed non-empty value \u2192 close edit mode\n  immediately (`setEditingId(null)`), call `onEdit(task.id, trimmed)`. This\n  is optimistic: the row briefly shows the old title until `App.jsx`'s\n  `run()` \u2192 `refresh()` completes, then shows the new one. No new\n  loading-state UI is introduced for this, matching Complete/Delete, which\n  have the same brief-old-value-until-refresh gap today.\n- **Save, oversized draft (AC5)** \u2014 no client-side length check is added\n  (spec non-goal). An over-200-char draft is *not* caught by the empty\n  check, so it takes the same path as a valid save: edit mode closes\n  optimistically, the request goes out, the backend 422s, and the existing\n  global banner in `App.jsx` shows it \u2014 identical to how `AddTask` handles\n  an oversized create today. This means AC5, unlike AC4, does *not* keep\n  edit mode open on rejection \u2014 that asymmetry is intentional: the spec says\n  AC5 should be rejected \"the same way create rejects it today,\" and create\n  has no such behavior either. If this asymmetry is undesirable, the fix is\n  a client-side length guard, which is explicitly out of scope (non-goal:\n  \"No character counter or other new max-length UI\").\n- **Click elsewhere on the page while editing** \u2014 no effect. Edit mode is\n  not exited by blur/click-outside; only explicit Cancel, Escape, Save, or\n  switching to another row's Edit closes it. (Not specified by the spec;\n  chosen because silent data loss on an accidental click is worse than\n  requiring an explicit action.)", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XtMdL6RnZNdJBDRuAEsfug", "session_id": "e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c"}}
