{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:16:24Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 213, "kind": "message", "text": "## Review \u2014 Taiga #2: Edit a task title\n\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 11 passed (backend). `npm run build` \u2192 clean. Read the full diff, `docs/spec.md`, and `docs/design.md` against it.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Disclosure, not a finding:** while testing the 422 response shape I created a scratch file `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` to inspect FastAPI's validation error body. It's untracked (`git status` confirms), and my sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on this session, so it's still sitting in the working tree. **Please delete `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` before committing** \u2014 it is not part of the developer's work.\n\n### Will block\n\nNone.\n\n### Will comment\n\nNone.\n\n### Worth considering\n\n1. **`frontend/src/api.js:8-11` (`request()`, unchanged by this diff) \u2014 oversized-title rejection (AC5) will render as `[object Object]`, not readable text.** FastAPI's 422 body puts `detail` as a *list* of validation-error objects, not a string (confirmed by hitting `PATCH` with a 201-char title: `{'detail': [{'type': 'string_too_long', ...}]}`). `request()` does `detail?.detail || ...` and throws `new Error(detail.detail)`, so `error.message` stringifies the array as `[object Object]` in the global banner. This is pre-existing (same path `AddTask` create already uses, `request()` itself is untouched by this diff), and `docs/design.md:64-71` explicitly reasons through this and accepts the asymmetry as intentional parity with create's existing behavior \u2014 so it's correctly out of scope for this cycle. Flagging only because AC5 says \"surfaced to the user,\" and today that surfacing is unreadable; worth a follow-up ticket on `request()`'s error formatting, not a blocker here.\n2. **No automated frontend test was added** for the new edit-mode UI (cancel/empty-rejection/save flows). Per the story stage's own note, `frontend/package.json` has no test framework installed despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test` \u2014 a pre-existing infra gap, not something this feature should fix solo, but it means AC1-5 (all frontend-only) are currently verified only by manual/design review, not a test suite. Worth a separate ticket to stand up frontend testing infra.\n\n### Spec/design conformance check (for the record)\n\nAll 8 ACs trace cleanly to the diff: AC1 (`startEdit`), AC2 (optimistic close + `run()`\u2192refresh), AC3 (`cancelEdit`, Escape handler), AC4 (client-side trim-guard, `role=\"alert\"`, edit mode stays open), AC5 (deliberately unguarded, per non-goal), AC6-8 (`backend/tests/test_tasks.py:42-60`, all passing). Both open questions from the spec (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode) are implemented as their stated defaults. No new component/color/pattern introduced beyond what `docs/design.md` scoped \u2014 reuses `AddTask`'s form/trim pattern and the existing error-banner path faithfully.\n\nVERDICT: approve-with-followups", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:16:24Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 214, "kind": "status", "text": "## Review \u2014 Taiga #2: Edit a task title\n\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 11 passed (backend). `npm run build` \u2192 clean. Read the full diff, `docs/spec.md`, and `docs/design.md` against it.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Disclosure, not a finding:** while testing the 422 response shape I created a scratch file `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` to inspect FastAPI's validation error body. It's untracked (`git status` confirms), and my sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on this session, so it's still sitting in the working tree. **Please delete `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` before committing** \u2014 it is not part of the developer's work.\n\n### Will block\n\nNone.\n\n### Will comment\n\nNone.\n\n### Worth considering\n\n1. **`frontend/src/api.js:8-11` (`request()`, unchanged by this diff) \u2014 oversized-title rejection (AC5) will render as `[object Object]`, not readable text.** FastAPI's 422 body puts `detail` as a *list* of validation-error objects, not a string (confirmed by hitting `PATCH` with a 201-char title: `{'detail': [{'type': 'string_too_long', ...}]}`). `request()` does `detail?.detail || ...` and throws `new Error(detail.detail)`, so `error.message` stringifies the array as `[object Object]` in the global banner. This is pre-existing (same path `AddTask` create already uses, `request()` itself is untouched by this diff), and `docs/design.md:64-71` explicitly reasons through this and accepts the asymmetry as intentional parity with create's existing behavior \u2014 so it's correctly out of scope for this cycle. Flagging only because AC5 says \"surfaced to the user,\" and today that surfacing is unreadable; worth a follow-up ticket on `request()`'s error formatting, not a blocker here.\n2. **No automated frontend test was added** for the new edit-mode UI (cancel/empty-rejection/save flows). Per the story stage's own note, `frontend/package.json` has no test framework installed despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test` \u2014 a pre-existing infra gap, not something this feature should fix solo, but it means AC1-5 (all frontend-only) are currently verified only by manual/design review, not a test suite. Worth a separate ticket to stand up frontend testing infra.\n\n### Spec/design conformance check (for the record)\n\nAll 8 ACs trace cleanly to the diff: AC1 (`startEdit`), AC2 (optimistic close + `run()`\u2192refresh), AC3 (`cancelEdit`, Escape handler), AC4 (client-side trim-guard, `role=\"alert\"`, edit mode stays open), AC5 (deliberately unguarded, per non-goal), AC6-8 (`backend/tests/test_tasks.py:42-60`, all passing). Both open questions from the spec (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode) are implemented as their stated defaults. No new component/color/pattern introduced beyond what `docs/design.md` scoped \u2014 reuses `AddTask`'s form/trim pattern and the existing error-banner path faithfully.\n\nVERDICT: approve-with-followups", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 1.0768340999999997}}
