{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:42:24Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 54, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "20\t## Acceptance criteria\n21\t\n22\t1. Given a task in the list, when the user activates edit mode for its title\n23\t   (an explicit \"Edit\" trigger, exact treatment the ux-designer's call), then\n24\t   the title becomes an editable input pre-filled with the task's current\n25\t   title.\n26\t2. Given a task in edit mode, when the user changes the text and confirms\n27\t   (Save), then the task's title is updated both via a backend call and in\n28\t   the UI, and edit mode closes showing the new title.\n29\t3. Given a task in edit mode, when the user cancels, then edit mode closes,\n30\t   the title reverts to its original value, and **no backend call is made**.\n31\t4. Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits with an empty title,\n32\t   then the edit is rejected: the task's title is **not** changed, no\n33\t   backend call that would wipe the title succeeds, and the user sees that\n34\t   the edit didn't go through (exact feedback \u2014 inline message vs. disabled\n35\t   Save \u2014 is the ux-designer's call, mirroring how `AddTask` disables `Add`\n36\t   until there's a trimmed, non-empty value).\n37\t5. Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits a title that is only\n38\t   whitespace, then it is treated the same as empty (criterion 4) \u2014 trimmed\n39\t   before the empty check, mirroring `AddTask.jsx`'s existing\n40\t   `title.trim()` guard.\n41\t6. Backend: a new endpoint accepts a title update for an existing task,\n42\t   reuses the existing `TaskIn` validation (`min_length=1, max_length=200`),\n43\t   and returns the updated `Task`.\n44\t7. Given the task id in the update request does not exist, then the backend\n45\t   returns `404`, matching the existing `complete_task`/`delete_task`\n46\t   pattern in `backend/app/main.py`.\n47\t8. Given a title update request with an empty string, then the backend\n48\t   returns `422` via the existing `TaskIn` field validation \u2014 same\n49\t   behaviour as `create_task` today (`test_empty_title_is_rejected` already\n50\t   covers the create path; the new route needs its own equivalent test).\n51\t9. Editing a task's title does not change its `done` state, position in the\n52\t   list, or any other field.\n53\t\n54\t## Non-goals\n55\t\n56\t- No inline editing of `done` state here \u2014 `Complete`/`Delete` buttons and\n57\t  their behaviour are unchanged.\n58\t- No bulk/multi-select editing.\n59\t- No edit history or undo beyond Cancel reverting the in-progress edit.\n60\t- No character counter or live remaining-length UI for the existing 200-char\n61\t  max \u2014 `AddTask` doesn't have one either, so this doesn't introduce a new\n62\t  pattern.\n63\t- No change to server-side whitespace handling on the **create** path\n64\t  (`POST /api/tasks`). It has the same latent quirk today (Pydantic's\n65\t  `min_length=1` counts raw characters, so a whitespace-only string\n66\t  technically passes) and this spec doesn't touch it \u2014 the edit path avoids\n67\t  the same problem by trimming client-side before submit, consistent with\n68\t  how `AddTask` already guards `Add`.\n69\t- No mandated keyboard shortcut (e.g. Escape-to-cancel) \u2014 a Cancel control\n70\t  satisfies criterion 3; whether to also wire Escape is the ux-designer's\n71\t  call, not a requirement here.\n72\t\n73\t## Affected areas\n74\t\n75\tBackend:\n76\t- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 new route, e.g. `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`,\n77\t  parallel in shape to `complete_task` (lines 32\u201337): look up via the store,\n78\t  404 if missing, return the updated `Task` on success. Request body reuses\n79\t  `TaskIn` (already has the right shape and validation \u2014 no new model\n80\t  needed).\n81\t- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 new method alongside `set_done` (lines 30\u201335),\n82\t  e.g. `update_title(task_id, title) -> Optional[Task]`, same\n83\t  found-or-`None` pattern.\n84\t- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 new tests for the route, in the same flat\n85\t  file as the existing route tests (that's the convention actually in use\n86\t  here \u2014 every existing route's tests live together in this one file,\n87\t  despite the `test_<route>.py`-per-route wording in `CLAUDE.md`; matching\n88\t  actual precedent over the literal doc).\n89\t\n90\tFrontend:\n91\t- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 new `updateTask(id, title)` calling the new PATCH\n92\t  endpoint, alongside the existing `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (lines\n93\t  20\u201321).\n94\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 each row needs edit-mode UI: a", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MQwCoxRzTh42S93AcipCtm", "session_id": "e57fba9e-0cb2-4bf7-b0c9-98e040eea1a9"}}
