{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:42:43Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 68, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "95\t  }\n96\t  return (\n97\t    <ul className=\"task-list\">\n98\t      {tasks.map((task) => (\n99\t        <TaskRow\n100\t          key={task.id}\n101\t          task={task}\n102\t          onComplete={onComplete}\n103\t          onDelete={onDelete}\n104\t          onUpdate={onUpdate}\n105\t        />\n106\t      ))}\n107\t    </ul>\n108\t  )\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\tfunction TaskRow({ task, onComplete, onDelete, onUpdate }) {\n112\t  const [isEditing, setIsEditing] = useState(false)\n113\t  const [draft, setDraft] = useState(task.title)\n114\t  const [showError, setShowError] = useState(false)\n115\t\n116\t  function startEdit() {\n117\t    setDraft(task.title)\n118\t    setShowError(false)\n119\t    setIsEditing(true)\n120\t  }\n121\t\n122\t  function cancel() {\n123\t    setDraft(task.title)\n124\t    setShowError(false)\n125\t    setIsEditing(false)\n126\t  }\n127\t\n128\t  function submit(e) {\n129\t    e.preventDefault()\n130\t    const trimmed = draft.trim()\n131\t    if (!trimmed) {\n132\t      setShowError(true)\n133\t      return\n134\t    }\n135\t    onUpdate(task.id, trimmed)\n136\t    setIsEditing(false)\n137\t  }\n138\t\n139\t  if (isEditing) {\n140\t    return (\n141\t      <li className={task.done ? 'task done' : 'task'}>\n142\t        <form className=\"task-edit\" onSubmit={submit} onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Escape' && cancel()}>\n143\t          <input\n144\t            className=\"task-title-input\"\n145\t            value={draft}\n146\t            onChange={(e) => { setDraft(e.target.value); setShowError(false) }}\n147\t            aria-label={`Title for ${task.title}`}\n148\t            autoFocus\n149\t            onFocus={(e) => e.target.select()}\n150\t          />\n151\t          <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>Save</button>\n152\t          <button type=\"button\" onClick={cancel}>Cancel</button>\n153\t        </form>\n154\t        {showError && <p className=\"field-error\" role=\"alert\">Title can't be empty</p>}\n155\t      </li>\n156\t    )\n157\t  }\n158\t\n159\t  return (\n160\t    <li className={task.done ? 'task done' : 'task'}>\n161\t      <span className=\"task-title\">{task.title}</span>\n162\t      <button onClick={startEdit} aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}>Edit</button>\n163\t      {!task.done && (\n164\t        <button onClick={() => onComplete(task.id)} aria-label={`Complete ${task.title}`}>Done</button>\n165\t      )}\n166\t      <button onClick={() => onDelete(task.id)} aria-label={`Delete ${task.title}`}>Delete</button>\n167\t    </li>\n168\t  )\n169\t}\n170\t```\n171\t\n172\t`onUpdate(id, title)` is fire-and-forget from `TaskRow`'s point of view \u2014\n173\tit doesn't await or handle failure locally; a failed save re-surfaces via\n174\t`App.jsx`'s existing `error` banner. `TaskRow` closes edit mode\n175\toptimistically on submit; if the backend call fails, `App.jsx`'s `refresh()`\n176\tnever runs (per `run()`'s `catch`), so `tasks` (and thus `task.title` passed\n177\tback into this row) stays at its last-known value \u2014 **not** the same as\n178\t\"edit mode stays open,\" see the follow-up note below.\n179\t\n180\t> **Note for developer:** the \"stays open on failure\" decision above only\n181\t> holds if `isEditing` isn't closed until `onUpdate` resolves. The sketch\n182\t> above closes immediately on submit (optimistic). Prefer awaiting\n183\t> `onUpdate` before calling `setIsEditing(false)`, closing edit mode only on\n184\t> success and leaving it open (with `draft` intact) if the call throws \u2014\n185\t> this matches the \"stays open on failure\" decision in the summary and is a\n186\t> small change to `submit()`: make it `async`, wrap the `onUpdate` call, and\n187\t> only `setIsEditing(false)` in the success path.\n188\t\n189\t## `api.js` change\n190\t\n191\t```js\n192\texport function updateTask(id, title) {\n193\t  return request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ title }) })\n194\t}\n195\t```\n196\t(Exact shape depends on `request`'s existing helper signature in\n197\t`frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 mirror `completeTask`/`deleteTask`'s call shape at\n198\tlines 20\u201321.)\n199\t\n200\t## `App.jsx` change\n201\t\n202\tAdd `onUpdate={(id, title) => run(() => api.updateTask(id, title))}` to the\n203\t`<TaskList>` call, alongside the existing `onComplete`/`onDelete` props\n204\t(lines 51\u201356) \u2014 identical wiring pattern, no new state in `App.jsx`.\n205\t\n206\t## `App.css` additions\n207\t\n208\t```css\n209\t.task-edit { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex: 1; align-items: center; }\n210\t.task-title-input {\n211\t  flex: 1;\n212\t  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;\n213\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n214\t  border-radius: 5px;\n215\t  font: inherit;\n216\t}\n217\t.task-title-input.invalid { border-color: #a3271d; }\n218\t.field-error {\n219\t  color: #a3271d;\n220\t  font-size: 0.85rem;\n221\t  margin: 0.3rem 0 0;\n222\t  flex-basis: 100%;\n223\t}\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t`.task-edit` reuses `.add-task`'s exact `display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;`\n227\trhythm. `.task-title-input` is `.add-task input`'s rule copied onto a class\n228\tusable inside a `<li>` (the existing rule is scoped to `.add-task input`,\n229\twhich wouldn't match here). `.field-error` reuses the existing `.error`\n230\tbanner's red (`#a3271d`) as plain text rather than the banner's pink chip\n231\tbackground \u2014 a full chip is disproportionate for a one-line per-field\n232\tmessage, and `error-placement` (below field) is the relevant guideline\n233\there, not the app-level banner treatment.\n234\t\n235\t`.task-title-input.invalid` is optional polish (red border on the input\n236\titself while `showError` is true, in addition to the text line) \u2014 include\n237\tit if trivial, skip it if it complicates `TaskRow`'s className logic; the\n238\ttext line alone already satisfies criterion 4 and `error-clarity`.\n239\t\n240\t## States\n241\t\n242\t### View (default row, unchanged shape + new Edit button)\n243\t\n244\t```\n245\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n246\t\u2502 Buy milk              [Edit][Done][Delete]   \u2502\n247\t\u2502 ~~Walk the dog~~            [Edit][Delete]   \u2502\n248\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n249\t```\n250\tMatches existing production row exactly, with `Edit` inserted before\n251\t`Done`/`Delete`. A done task still has no `Done` button (existing\n252\tbehavior, unchanged) but does get `Edit` \u2014 editing title is independent of\n253\t`done` state (criterion 9).\n254\t\n255\t### Edit mode entered (AC 1) \u2014 populated, pre-filled\n256\t\n257\t```\n258\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n259\t\u2502 [ Buy milk|.....................] [Save][Cancel] \u2502\n260\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n261\t```\n262\t`|` marks the caret; input is autofocused with existing text selected.\n263\t`Save` is enabled (draft is non-empty and unchanged from `task.title`, a\n264\tvalid no-op save per spec's edge cases).", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FiqNfpUpu4wuVvPDC1CoTD", "session_id": "e57fba9e-0cb2-4bf7-b0c9-98e040eea1a9"}}
