{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:44:27Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 150, "kind": "message", "text": "## Review: Taiga #3 \u2014 Edit a task title\n\n**Verified, not just read:**\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 12/12 passed\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 succeeds\n- `python3 -m pytest e2e/ -q` \u2192 28/28 passed (including all 9 new edit-title scenarios: prefill, save, save-closes-edit, cancel-reverts-no-backend-call, disabled-Save-on-empty, Enter-rejects-empty, Enter-rejects-whitespace, done-state-preserved)\n\nNote: the handoff text claimed the developer \"stayed strictly in backend/... frontend is out of my scope \u2014 not touched,\" but the actual diff includes substantial frontend changes (`TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, e2e tests). I disregarded that claim and reviewed/tested the code as it actually stands rather than as reported \u2014 flagging this only so the orchestrator is aware the stage report doesn't match the diff, though the code itself is sound.\n\n**Will block:** none.\n\n**Will comment:** none.\n\n**Worth considering:**\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`'s `onKeyDown` Enter handler is a deliberate, commented deviation from `docs/design.md`'s sketch (which only wired Escape). It's correct \u2014 a disabled Save button blocks native implicit form-submission-on-Enter, so this is required to make AC5 (whitespace-only via Enter) actually surface the inline error \u2014 and it's proven by the passing e2e tests. Flagging only as a documented deviation, not a defect.\n- The server-side whitespace-only quirk (`TaskIn`'s `min_length=1` counts raw characters, so `\"   \"` would pass Pydantic on a direct API call) is *not* fixed by this PR \u2014 but that's an explicit, spec-documented non-goal (`docs/spec.md:63-68`), consistent with the same pre-existing quirk on `create`, and the UI-facing path is fully guarded client-side (trimmed before submit) and tested server-side for the true-empty case. Not a gap in this feature's actual acceptance criteria.\n\nAll 9 acceptance criteria in `docs/spec.md` are covered by tests and pass. Backend mirrors `set_done`'s exact pattern; frontend reuses `.add-task`'s existing styles and `AddTask`'s trim-guard idiom. No scope creep, no unjustified surface added.\n\nVERDICT: approve", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "e57fba9e-0cb2-4bf7-b0c9-98e040eea1a9"}}
